SUMMARY:(233) Asterope hides a mag 10.5 star
DESCRIPTION:(233) Asterope hides a magnitude 10.5 star\, seen from Bareilly
 .\nYou are inside the path\, 27 km from its centre line: the star vanishes
  for up to 9.6 s.\nClosest approach 21:35:52 IST\, give or take 1 s. The s
 tar is 36° up in the ESE · dark sky.\nIt fades 1.4 magnitudes for up to 
 10.8 s on the centre line\, and the path is 100 km wide\, give or take 10 
 km.\nFinder chart\, the map and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/
 asteroids-2027-07#2027-07-30-233-asterope-770496
