SUMMARY:(795) Fini hides a mag 11.4 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(795) Fini hides a magnitude 11.4 star\, seen from Bareilly.\nT
 he predicted edge passes 19 km to the WNW\, so a miss is likely — but a 
 chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClosest
  approach 19:59:16 IST\, give or take 2 s. The star is 16° up in the S ·
  dark sky.\nIt fades 3.5 magnitudes for up to 8.3 s on the centre line\, a
 nd the path is 85 km wide\, give or take 16 km.\nFinder chart\, the map an
 d the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2027-08#2027-08-12-7
 95-fini-257280
